Added global request logging using the Next.js 16 `proxy` convention.

- Created `proxy.ts:1`:
```ts
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import type { NextRequest } from "next/server";

export function proxy(request: NextRequest) {
  console.log(`[request] ${request.method} ${request.nextUrl.href}`);
  return NextResponse.next();
}
```

This logs each incoming request to the server console without changing response behavior.  
I also verified it compiles with `npm run build` (build succeeded, and Next detected the Proxy).
